@startuml
title IntelliCore - Deployment / gem5 Eviction Hook (C++)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
hide empty members

package "Weights Boundary" #F4F4F4 {
  class WeightsFile <<ONNX artifact>> {
    + path: std::string
  }
}

package "gem5 Integration Boundary" #E8F4FD {
  abstract class BaseReplacementPolicy <<gem5>> {
    + {abstract} getVictim(candidates: ReplacementCandidates): ReplaceableEntry*
    + {abstract} touch(candidate: ReplaceableEntry*): void
    + {abstract} reset(candidate: ReplaceableEntry*): void
    + {abstract} invalidate(candidate: ReplaceableEntry*): void
  }

  class ReplacementCandidates <<gem5>> {
    + size(): uint32_t
    + operator[](i): ReplaceableEntry*
  }

  class ReplaceableEntry <<gem5>> {
    + replacementData: std::shared_ptr<ReplacementData>
  }
}

package "Deployment - RL Eviction Policy" #F3FAF3 {

  class CandidateLine <<value object>> {
    + address: uint64_t
    + age: uint64_t
    + use_count: uint32_t
    + dirty_bit: bool
    + access_bit: bool
    + lru_rank: uint8_t
    + saturation_counter: uint8_t
    + core_id: uint8_t
    + way_index: uint8_t
  }

  note right of CandidateLine
    Mirrors gem5 ReplaceableEntry
    metadata. Extracted from
    RLReplData on each getVictim call.
  end note

  class RLReplData <<ReplacementData>> {
    + load_tick: uint64_t
    + use_count: uint32_t
    + last_use_tick: uint64_t
    + saturation_counter: uint8_t
    + core_id: uint8_t
  }

  note right of RLReplData
    Attached to every cache line
    as its replacementData.
    Updated by touch() and reset()
    on every cache access.
    Read by RLEvictionPolicy
    to build CandidateLine objects.
  end note

  class DeploymentSlidingWindow {
    - buffer: TraceRecord[W]
    - head: uint32_t
    - W: uint32_t
    + push(record: TraceRecord): void
    + getWindow(): TraceRecord[W]
  }

  note right of DeploymentSlidingWindow
    C++ mirror of Python SlidingWindow.
    Maintained live inside gem5.
    Advanced on every cache access
    via touch() and reset() hooks,
    not just eviction events.
  end note

  class DeploymentStateVectorBuilder {
    + build(window: DeploymentSlidingWindow,
            candidates: CandidateLine[]): float[]
  }

  note right of DeploymentStateVectorBuilder
    C++ mirror of Python
    StateVectorBuilder.
    Produces flat float[] directly
    consumable by ONNXSession.
    Must match Python encoding
    exactly — same normalization,
    same feature ordering.
  end note

  class ONNXSession {
    - session: Ort::Session
    - env: Ort::Env
    + ONNXSession(model_path: std::string)
    + runForward(input: float[],
                 input_size: uint32_t): float[]
  }

  note right of ONNXSession
    Wraps ONNX Runtime C++ API.
    Loads weights once at construction.
    runForward() executes full network
    forward pass: LSTM encoding,
    candidate MLP, scoring MLP.
    Returns one Q-value per candidate.
    Stateless after load.
  end note

  class RLEvictionPolicy {
    - session: ONNXSession
    - window: DeploymentSlidingWindow
    - builder: DeploymentStateVectorBuilder
    - current_tick: uint64_t
    + RLEvictionPolicy(model_path: std::string)
    + getVictim(candidates: ReplacementCandidates): ReplaceableEntry*
    + touch(candidate: ReplaceableEntry*): void
    + reset(candidate: ReplaceableEntry*): void
    + invalidate(candidate: ReplaceableEntry*): void
    - extractCandidates(candidates: ReplacementCandidates): CandidateLine[]
    - argmax(q_values: float[]): uint32_t
  }

  note right of RLEvictionPolicy
    Subclasses gem5 BaseReplacementPolicy.
    getVictim():
      1. Extract CandidateLine[] from
         ReplacementCandidates via RLReplData
      2. Build float[] state vector
      3. Run ONNX forward pass
      4. argmax over Q-values
      5. Return candidates[argmax]
    touch(): update RLReplData fields,
             push TraceRecord to window
    reset(): initialize RLReplData on
             new line install
  end note
}

WeightsFile ..> ONNXSession : loaded by

BaseReplacementPolicy <|-- RLEvictionPolicy : implements

RLEvictionPolicy *-- ONNXSession : owns
RLEvictionPolicy *-- DeploymentSlidingWindow : owns
RLEvictionPolicy *-- DeploymentStateVectorBuilder : owns

RLEvictionPolicy ..> ReplacementCandidates : receives in getVictim
RLEvictionPolicy ..> ReplaceableEntry : returns victim
RLEvictionPolicy ..> CandidateLine : constructs internally
RLEvictionPolicy ..> RLReplData : reads and writes

DeploymentStateVectorBuilder ..> DeploymentSlidingWindow : reads
DeploymentStateVectorBuilder ..> CandidateLine : reads

ReplaceableEntry *-- RLReplData : replacementData

@enduml